      "explanation": "First simplify the recurrence:\n\\[\nF(n+1)=\\frac{2F(n)+1}{2}=F(n)+\\frac12.\n\\]\nThus every increase of 1 in the index adds \\(\\frac12\\) to the value. Going from \\(F(1)\\) to \\(F(101)\\) takes \\(101-1=100\\) such increases, so\n\\[\nF(101)=2+100\\left(\\frac12\\right)=\\boxed{52}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice D.",
